Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: block unsafe generic MT7987 DVFS

Revalidated base: Frank-W Linux 6.18.52
(a638fabe36f293e58ab6be002af04b866959c546).

Replace the E87N 6.12 fixed-voltage/MT7987 patches 843/844 with an
explicitly disabled CPUFreq path pending validated board supply and OPP
data. The old DTS has no proc-supply and gives all four frequencies,
500 MHz through 2 GHz, the same 850 mV. Skipping set_voltage neither
satisfies the mandatory proc regulator lookup nor proves voltage safety.
The old platform data also leaves min_volt_shift zero, which the 6.18.51
driver uses unconditionally as the voltage-tracking divisor.

The board config disables CPU_FREQ regardless of maintained driver matches.
Block cpufreq-dt's OPP-v2 auto-registration too, so keeping an
old OPP table cannot silently select a generic clock-only transition
without the MediaTek intermediate-clock sequencing.

The board DTS must retain the mediatek,mt7987 root compatible, omit
unvalidated CPU OPP references/tables and CPUFreq cooling maps, and keep
polled thermal zones and critical trips. CPU frequency/voltage remain
under the existing firmware/clock setup, without Linux DVFS. This is a
safety restriction, not functional CPUFreq support.

---

--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c
@@ -134,6 +134,8 @@
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt2712", },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt7622", },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt7623", },
+	/* MT7987 has no validated CPU supply/OPPs or safe generic clock path. */
+	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt7987", },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt8167", },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt817x", },
 	{ .compatible = "mediatek,mt8173", },
